                <pb facs="0227" n="99" xml:id="pg99"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 67.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1885-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 2, 1885</date>. (Received April 16.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Hall informs the Department that a battle was fought to day (the 2d) between
                    the forces of Salvador and Guatemala, in which the President of Guatemala was
                    killed. He says the diplomatic corps has proposed an armistice.</p>
            </div>
